SHOT: A warm animated family drama with a quiet wonder: in the hall Rosa draws the violet stick from her bag and shows Michelle how it turns from white into her own shade; one take of 5 shots, 9:16, 17 s.

TIMELINE
[0–4s] Shot 1 · medium, slider moving sideways: Frame 1: Rosa and Michelle face to face under the pendant, Rosa's bag on her shoulder — her hand goes into the bag and comes out with the stick; the slider moves a little sideways. Rosa says: "This is the one that changed it for me."
[4–7s] Shot 2 · insert, pull-out from the macro: the camera pulls out from the wordmark to the whole stick in her hand; the light slides down the barrel. Rosa says: "Here, let me just show you."
[7–11s] Shot 3 · medium close-up, slow creep in: one stroke of the balm across the cheek; Michelle's eyes flick to it. Rosa says: "It comes out pure white."
[11–14s] Shot 4 · medium, slow pan: the stick turns in her fingers; the pan follows it up to her face. Rosa says: "Then it reads the warmth of your own skin"
[14–17s] Shot 5 · close-up, slow creep in: Rosa lifts the brush end toward the stripe; the camera creeps in. Rosa says: "and turns into your exact shade, and it melts right in." Last frame: Rosa and Michelle face to face under the pendant, the white stripe on Michelle's cheek, the brush end of the stick in Rosa's hand.

LOOK: A theatrical 3D animated feature, stylised adults with large expressive eyes, soft skin, sculpted hair, fabric with weight; natural, ungraded colour; light from the globe pendant light in the hall, a shadow side on every face. Rosa: the marigold-orange wrap blouse and long ink-blue skirt, tan sandals; Michelle: an old oversized faded-grey sweatshirt over charcoal pull-on trousers, grey felt slippers, hair limp.

SOUND: Dialogue in natural American English — Rosa's voice from @audio1; only the person written as speaking speaks, and on every other shot nobody speaks. No music. The actions' own sounds: the bag's zip, the cap coming off the stick, the soft brush on skin; the quiet hall at night under it.

KEEP: same faces, hair and clothes in every frame; just Rosa and Michelle in the scene; exactly one violet stick at its true size, its wordmark the only text; five fingers on each hand; real weight and timing; eyes off the lens; every line of her skin stays exactly as deep; only the colour evens out

