SHOT: A warm animated close: on the patio in the late sun Michelle turns to us, holds up the violet stick and tells us it was never us; one take of 6 shots, 9:16, 22 s.

TIMELINE
[0–4s] Shot 1 · medium close-up, slow push-in: Frame 1: Michelle seated at the patio table by the lemon tree in the late sun, looking at the garden wall, her violet stick on the table — her head turns from the garden to the lens; the camera pushes in slowly. Michelle says: "So if someone ever looked at you and made you feel like you had faded,"
[4–7s] Shot 2 · close-up, slow creep in: she leans an inch toward the lens and nods once; the camera creeps in. A beat of stillness first. Michelle says: "please hear me. It was never you."
[7–11s] Shot 3 · medium, slow pan: her hand lifts the stick up beside her cheek; the pan follows it. Michelle says: "The thing she wanted to know, I will tell you instead."
[11–14s] Shot 4 · medium close-up, slider moving sideways: she turns the stick so the wordmark faces the lens; the slider glides sideways. Michelle says: "It is called FACELOVE, and I have linked it below."
[14–18s] Shot 5 · close-up, slow creep in: the stick lowers, the smile widens, a breeze moves her hair; the camera creeps in.
[18–22s] Shot 6 · full shot, leading her, backing away in front: she stands up and walks three steps to the bougainvillea; the camera leads her. Last frame: Michelle standing by the bougainvillea in the late sun, the stick in her hand.

